{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-10399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-10399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\nx\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})+1,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\ne n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & \\ne n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-10399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d9469834491df564b8431873264b245b6e82af9725be824c0ddfc255a3fabada"} {"question" "q-10399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-10399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ne \\frac{3\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+3n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-10399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-29438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-29438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ This gives\n\n$$\nx-\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-\\frac{\\pi }{3} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-29438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d9469834491df564b8431873264b245b6e82af9725be824c0ddfc255a3fabada"} {"question" "q-29438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-29438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-29438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-81553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function  $f(x)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-81553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-81553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d9469834491df564b8431873264b245b6e82af9725be824c0ddfc255a3fabada"} {"question" "q-81553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-81553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+4n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{8}"] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2n\\pi "] ["math" "x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-81553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function  $f(x)=2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)-5,$  where \n$x$ is measured in degrees? Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=n\\cdot {180}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $2\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x)-5,$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x=n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =n\\cdot {180}^{∘} \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\cdot {180}^{∘}}{3} \\\\ x & =n\\cdot {60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=n\\cdot {60}^{∘},$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d9469834491df564b8431873264b245b6e82af9725be824c0ddfc255a3fabada"} {"question" "q-117692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=n\\cdot {120}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=n\\cdot {20}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=n\\cdot {30}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=n\\cdot {60}^{∘}"] ["math" "x=n\\cdot {90}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117692" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=n\\cdot {60}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the domain of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The domain of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ is given by the expression\n\n$$\nx\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the domain of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(4x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n4x+\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+\\frac{\\pi }{6} & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 4x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ 4x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot 4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4} \\\\ x & \\ne \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the function is $x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4},$ where $n$ is an integer." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117706" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d9469834491df564b8431873264b245b6e82af9725be824c0ddfc255a3fabada"} {"question" "q-117706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037965/state.json" "file_sha256" "8f51ffa9c761963f3aa16e265ec5ee5676594340c4489e0bb696e0ede63deb6e"} {"question" "q-117706" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{n\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "x\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{n\\pi }{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Aca